<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">20 April in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">5 events that happened on 20 April, from 1534 to 1999.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/jacques-cartier" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jacques-cartier.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1534 CE <span class="tih-ago">492 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Jacques Cartier sails from Saint-Malo for North America</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Jacques Cartier left Brittany on the first of three voyages that explored the Gulf of St Lawrence. His expeditions laid the basis for France's later claim to Canada.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/french-empire">French Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jacques-cartier">Jacques Cartier</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-america">North America</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canada">Canada</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1653 CE <span class="tih-ago">373 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Oliver Cromwell dissolves the Rump Parliament</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Cromwell entered the Commons with musketeers and expelled the remaining members. The act paved the way for his rule as Lord Protector later that year.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1657 CE <span class="tih-ago">369 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Robert Blake destroys a Spanish fleet at Santa Cruz de Tenerife</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Admiral Robert Blake sailed into the defended harbour and burned the Spanish ships sheltering there without losing a vessel of his own. It was one of the boldest naval actions of the age.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1792 CE <span class="tih-ago">234 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">France declares war on Austria</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Legislative Assembly voted for war against the Habsburg monarch, opening the French Revolutionary Wars. Conflict between France and the European powers would last, almost unbroken, until 1815.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-revolutionary-wars">French Revolutionary Wars</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1999 CE <span class="tih-ago">27 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Two students kill 13 people at Columbine High School</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Two students at the Colorado school shot dead twelve classmates and a teacher before killing themselves. The attack transformed school security and police response tactics across the United States.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a></div></div></li></ol>
